      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: what did nadi mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: చెరువు",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "చెరువు (ceruvu) — \"a village tank, a reservoir\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A చెరువు (ceruvu) is not a natural lake. It is a dug and banked tank that catches the rain and holds it through the dry months, and a great many Telugu villages were laid out around one before they were laid out around anything else."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "So the word carries an argument about how the country was settled: the నది (nadi) is where the water goes, the చెరువు (ceruvu) is where it was made to stay. Kings had them dug and put their names on the bunds, and the names are still there."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Indian English calls this a \"tank\", which is why the translation can sound strange until you have stood on the bund of one."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two waters: one that moves, one that was kept."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "ceruvu",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *ceruvu*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "ceruvu, then nadi, and say which one people made",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *ceruvu*, then *nadi*, and say which one people made]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
