        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: బాట",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "బాట (bāṭa) — \"a path, a way\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "బాట (bāṭa) is the inherited word for a way, a track, the line worn by feet going the same way twice. దారి does much the same work; బాట (bāṭa) is the more physical of the two, the ground itself."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It goes abstract as easily as English \"path\" does. బాట (bāṭa) పట్టు is to take up a way of living, and a person can be on somebody else's బాట (bāṭa)."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You can now ask your way properly: దయచేసి, which గ్రామం (grāmaṁ), which బాట (bāṭa), which side the నది (nadi) is on."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five: నది (nadi), చెరువు (ceruvu), గుట్ట (guṭṭa), గ్రామం (grāmaṁ), బాట (bāṭa). Enough to be given directions with."
            }
          ]
        },
